# rt_* -> typed std alias map (rt migration programme, base c42a57bb94d, generated 2026-08-28).
# class: same     = alias with identical signature+semantics (mechanically rewritable by rt_migrate)
#        adapted  = wrapper exists but transforms args/return; hand migration
#        provider = genuine runtime boundary; stays a direct call inside an allowlisted provider
#        missing  = no alias and none could be generated (see note)
# decl: the extern signature the alias is identical to (param names irrelevant; unit/void/none equal).
# variants: additional (decl -> alias) pairs for symbols whose legacy decls disagree on a type.
# Coverage of the 892 covered symbols: same=480(24631 sites) adapted=6(180 sites) provider=383(7083 sites) missing=23(194 sites)
# 2026-09-02: 5 entries reclassified same->missing (rt_host_wm_client_poll_event, rt_host_wm_client_request,
#   rt_mem_attr_report, rt_mem_harden_check, rt_mem_read_u8): none names a native symbol (Rust extern "C" fn or a
#   src/runtime C definition), so their generated wrappers in src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/sffi/platform.spl were undefined
#   at link -- MSVC LNK2019/LNK1120 in Stage 2. lld tolerates undefined symbols, which is why Linux never saw it.
